Package: climatXL
Title: Non-Stationary Extreme Value Pricing of Catastrophe Excess-of-Loss Reinsurance
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Yassine", "", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "yassine@example.com")
Description: Tools to test whether the distribution of extreme catastrophe
    losses changes over time and with climate indices, and to translate the
    answer into an excess-of-loss reinsurance premium. Provides peaks-over-
    threshold tools (mean excess plot, Hill estimator, generalised Pareto
    maximum likelihood fit, return levels, Value-at-Risk and expected
    shortfall), validated against McNeil (1997) on the Danish fire losses.
